2026-10-15 12:09:36 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:09:36 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer'], 'text': "I'll design this agent network. Since the request describes a generic domain (document redaction with PII/PHI compliance) rather than a specific named organization, I'll proceed directly to structuring the network, grounding it in standard redaction and data-privacy workflows.\n\nLet me start by creating the network structure."}
2026-10-15 12:09:36 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:09:36 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer'], 'text': 'Invoking: `__agent_network_editor` with:\n{"invoking_start": true, "invoked_agent_name": "__agent_network_editor", "params": {"agent_network_description": "Create an agent network for a secure, privacy-compliant, human-in-the-loop (HITL) document redaction and obfuscation system with active learning. The system handles sensitive documents containing PII/PHI and must guarantee no unapproved content is released.\\n\\nCore workflows and required agents:\\n\\n1) INGESTION & PAGINATION AGENT - Accepts uploaded text files (.txt, .md, .csv, raw text streams). Chunks/paginates input into deterministic, page-bounded logical units (fixed, reproducible page boundaries) so each page can be processed and approved individually. Emits an ordered list of page objects with stable page_ids and source offsets.\\n\\n2) MASTER CLASSIFIER REPOSITORY AGENT (GOVERNANCE STORE) - Maintains a centralized, editable \\"Master Data Classifiers\\" store: PII/PHI categories, regular expressions, named entity types (NER types), and confidence thresholds. This is the single source of truth for detection rules. It exposes an ADMIN-GATED mutation interface: no classifier rule can be added, modified, or removed without explicit Human Admin approval. Read access is unrestricted; write access is gated.\\n\\n3) CLASSIFICATION & DETECTION AGENT - Loads the active classifier ruleset from the Master Classifier Repository and scans each page, producing candidate target spans with category labels, matched rule IDs, and confidence scores. Applies confidence thresholds to decide which spans to surface.\\n\\n4) REDACTION RENDERING AGENT - From a page\'s detected spans, generates DUAL STATE OUTPUTS: (a) Unredacted State with AI-highlighted target spans (with span offsets + labels), and (b) Redacted State with mask tokens/characters applied. Produces both states for side-by-side human review.\\n\\n5) HITL GATEWAY / HUMAN REVIEW INTERCEPT AGENT - Presents the side-by-side view to the Human Operator and PAUSES execution at every page boundary. Collects explicit Human Operator feedback per page: Approve as-is, Modify redaction spans (add/remove highlights), or Reject and flag for re-classification. Enforces the hard gate: execution MUST NOT progress to page N+1 until page N receives approval. Maintains the approval matrix.\\n\\n6) FEEDBACK LOGGING AGENT - Logs all human modifications with context: additions = false negatives, removals = false positives. Records the context snippet, active classifier ID, page_id, and span offsets into a feedback buffer/log. Routes feedback to the Active Learning Agent.\\n\\n7) ACTIVE LEARNING AGENT (GOVERNANCE/LEARNING) - Periodically synthesizes error patterns from feedback logs and outputs recommended updates (new rules, threshold adjustments, regex/NER changes) for the Master Data Classifiers. These are only PROPOSALS; they are routed to Human Admin review and never applied automatically.\\n\\n8) FINAL OBFUSCATION & ENCODING AGENT - Completion gate: document status stays \\"IN_PROGRESS\\" until 100% of pages are approved. Upon full approval, assembles and renders a brand-new, hardened obfuscated file that strips all source metadata and original text layers, rendering the obfuscation cryptographically/structurally irreversible.\\n\\n9) ORCHESTRATOR / SUPERVISOR AGENT - Top-level coordinator. Owns the shared network state (document_status, current_page_index, approval_matrix, feedback_buffer, trip binding). Drives the sequential page loop, invokes the HITL gate at each boundary, and triggers final encoding only when the completion gate is satisfied.\\n\\nInter-agent communication: Orchestrator dispatches to Ingestion -> Classifier -> Redaction Renderer -> HITL Gateway per page; HITL feedback flows to Feedback Logging -> Active Learning -> (proposal) -> Master Classifier Repository (admin-gated); approval flows back to Orchestrator to advance the page pointer; Final Encoder is invoked by Orchestrator on completion.\\n\\nThis network must be deterministic, privacy-safe, and enforce human oversight at every irreversible step.", "mode": "create"}}'}
2026-10-15 12:09:36 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:09:36 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer', '/agent_network_editor'], 'text': 'Received arguments:\n{"tool_start": true, "tool_args": {"agent_network_description": "Create an agent network for a secure, privacy-compliant, human-in-the-loop (HITL) document redaction and obfuscation system with active learning. The system handles sensitive documents containing PII/PHI and must guarantee no unapproved content is released.\\n\\nCore workflows and required agents:\\n\\n1) INGESTION & PAGINATION AGENT - Accepts uploaded text files (.txt, .md, .csv, raw text streams). Chunks/paginates input into deterministic, page-bounded logical units (fixed, reproducible page boundaries) so each page can be processed and approved individually. Emits an ordered list of page objects with stable page_ids and source offsets.\\n\\n2) MASTER CLASSIFIER REPOSITORY AGENT (GOVERNANCE STORE) - Maintains a centralized, editable \\"Master Data Classifiers\\" store: PII/PHI categories, regular expressions, named entity types (NER types), and confidence thresholds. This is the single source of truth for detection rules. It exposes an ADMIN-GATED mutation interface: no classifier rule can be added, modified, or removed without explicit Human Admin approval. Read access is unrestricted; write access is gated.\\n\\n3) CLASSIFICATION & DETECTION AGENT - Loads the active classifier ruleset from the Master Classifier Repository and scans each page, producing candidate target spans with category labels, matched rule IDs, and confidence scores. Applies confidence thresholds to decide which spans to surface.\\n\\n4) REDACTION RENDERING AGENT - From a page\'s detected spans, generates DUAL STATE OUTPUTS: (a) Unredacted State with AI-highlighted target spans (with span offsets + labels), and (b) Redacted State with mask tokens/characters applied. Produces both states for side-by-side human review.\\n\\n5) HITL GATEWAY / HUMAN REVIEW INTERCEPT AGENT - Presents the side-by-side view to the Human Operator and PAUSES execution at every page boundary. Collects explicit Human Operator feedback per page: Approve as-is, Modify redaction spans (add/remove highlights), or Reject and flag for re-classification. Enforces the hard gate: execution MUST NOT progress to page N+1 until page N receives approval. Maintains the approval matrix.\\n\\n6) FEEDBACK LOGGING AGENT - Logs all human modifications with context: additions = false negatives, removals = false positives. Records the context snippet, active classifier ID, page_id, and span offsets into a feedback buffer/log. Routes feedback to the Active Learning Agent.\\n\\n7) ACTIVE LEARNING AGENT (GOVERNANCE/LEARNING) - Periodically synthesizes error patterns from feedback logs and outputs recommended updates (new rules, threshold adjustments, regex/NER changes) for the Master Data Classifiers. These are only PROPOSALS; they are routed to Human Admin review and never applied automatically.\\n\\n8) FINAL OBFUSCATION & ENCODING AGENT - Completion gate: document status stays \\"IN_PROGRESS\\" until 100% of pages are approved. Upon full approval, assembles and renders a brand-new, hardened obfuscated file that strips all source metadata and original text layers, rendering the obfuscation cryptographically/structurally irreversible.\\n\\n9) ORCHESTRATOR / SUPERVISOR AGENT - Top-level coordinator. Owns the shared network state (document_status, current_page_index, approval_matrix, feedback_buffer, trip binding). Drives the sequential page loop, invokes the HITL gate at each boundary, and triggers final encoding only when the completion gate is satisfied.\\n\\nInter-agent communication: Orchestrator dispatches to Ingestion -> Classifier -> Redaction Renderer -> HITL Gateway per page; HITL feedback flows to Feedback Logging -> Active Learning -> (proposal) -> Master Classifier Repository (admin-gated); approval flows back to Orchestrator to advance the page pointer; Final Encoder is invoked by Orchestrator on completion.\\n\\nThis network must be deterministic, privacy-safe, and enforce human oversight at every irreversible step.", "mode": "create", "toolbox": null, "subnetwork": null, "mcp_tool": null}}'}
