2026-10-15 12:10:44 BST | INFO     | NeuroSan:_log:821 - NeuroSan - {"message": "Done with agent_network_designer.StreamingChat request for 'Design an agent network for - ### GOAL Build a secure, privacy-compliant, human-in-the-loop (HITL) document redaction and obfuscation agent network with active learning capabilities. --- ### NETWORK REQUIREMENTS & BEHAVIORAL SPECIFICATION 1. DOCUMENT INGESTION & PAGINATION - Accept uploaded text files (e.g., .txt, .md, .csv, raw text streams). - Chunk/paginate input text into deterministic, page-bounded logical units for granular per-page processing. 2. MASTER CLASSIFICATION REPOSITORY (GOVERNANCE) - Maintain a centralized, editable "Master Data Classifiers" store (containing PII/PHI categories, regular expressions, named entity types, and confidence thresholds). - The AI network can analyze false positives/negatives and PROPOSE rule/classifier updates. - MANDATORY GATE: No master classifier rule can be modified, added, or removed without explicit Human Admin approval. 3. PAGE-BY-PAGE HITL REDACTION ENGINE - Process pages sequentially. - For each page, generate dual state outputs: * Unredacted State (with AI-highlighted target spans) * Redacted State (with mask tokens/characters applied) - Present a side-by-side view to the Human Operator. - PAUSE EXECUTION at every page boundary. Require explicit Human Operator feedback: * Approve page as-is * Modify redaction spans (add/remove highlights) * Reject and flag for re-classification - The execution loop MUST NOT progress to page (N+1) until page (N) receives human approval. 4. IRREVERSIBLE OBFUSCATION & FINAL ENCODING - Process completion gate: Document status remains "IN_PROGRESS" until 100% of pages are approved. - Upon full approval, assemble and render a brand-new, hardened obfuscated file. - Ensure the final output strips all source metadata and original text layers, rendering the obfuscation cryptographically/structurally irreversible. 5. FEEDBACK LOGGING & CONTINUOUS ACTIVE LEARNING - Log all human modifications (additions = false negatives; removals = false positives) alongside the context snippet and active classifier ID. - Route feedback logs to a learning sub-agent that periodically synthesizes error patterns and outputs recommended updates for the Master Data Classifiers. --- ### REQUIRED ARCHITECTURAL DELIVERABLES Please generate the following design blueprints: 1. Agent Topology & Network Graph: Define each specialized agent (e.g., Ingestion Agent, Classifier Agent, Redaction Rendering Agent, Governance/Learning Agent) and their inter-agent communication channels. 2. State Schema & Flow Control: Detail the shared network state (document status, current_page_index, approval_matrix, feedback_buffer) and conditional transition logic. 3. HITL Intercept Points: Define the exact interruption state and UI payload contract required for the side-by-side human review tool. 4. Active Learning Loop Protocol: Define how feedback data is processed to generate suggested classifier updates for human review.'", "user_id": "snigdhasahoo", "Timestamp": "2026-10-15T12:10:44.902731", "source": "HttpServer", "message_type": "Other", "request_id": "request-4"}
