the accumulated structured feedback to the learning stage. I do not decide, approve, or apply any classifier change.",\n        "Clarification requested: is the ask (a) to log the raw MODIFY/REJECT operator edits as append-only structured records (my scope, partial), or (b) to run the live presentation/halt loop and populate the approval matrix (not my scope)? If (a), route each captured edit to me as it occurs; if I am to preserve an APPROVE with no span change, confirm how the matrix encodes it, since my record schema is oriented to ADD/REMOVE span edits and REJECT."\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n**Summary:** I am partially relevant. I do not present pages or run the `WAITING_FOR_HUMAN` state machine, and I do not write the approval matrix. My role is the feedback-logging stage: converting each captured operator MODIFY (ADD/REMOVE) or REJECT edit into an append-only structured training record and forwarding it to the learning stage. I also called my down-chain agent (Active Learning Agent), which confirmed it is only relevant to the downstream, batch/periodic aggregation of already-recorded decisions — not to live presentation, halting, or matrix population.\n\nTwo follow-ups needed: (1) clarify whether the ask is scope (a) or (b); (2) resolve the `write_file` allow-list failure so records can be durably persisted.'}
