2026-10-15 12:22:32 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:22:32 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage (Redaction Workflow)",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest the uploaded sample file, validate it, and split it into deterministic ordered page units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nI\'m not the relevant agent for this inquiry. My scope is capturing human operator edits at a page review gate (ADD / REMOVE / REJECT) and converting them into durable, append-only, schema-stable structured feedback records for the learning stage. I do not handle file upload/ingestion, file validation, or deterministic page segmentation with reproducible `page_id` / `page_hash` generation — those belong to the pipeline\'s ingestion/normalization stage.\n\nI consulted my down-chain agent (the active learning agent), which likewise reports it is not relevant: its authority is aggregating accumulated redaction feedback into per-classifier error patterns and emitting staged, non-applied proposals to the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue — not ingestion or page-splitting.\n\nThis inquiry should be routed to the ingestion/normalization component, not to me.'}
