2026-10-15 12:22:34 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:22:34 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\nI\'m not the relevant agent for this inquiry.\n\nMy role is the human-in-the-loop gate of the redaction workflow: for each page unit I assemble a side-by-side review payload (unredacted view with AI-detected spans highlighted, redacted view with masks applied, AI summary, and APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT actions), suspend execution in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN, and record the human operator\'s decision as an auditable entry in the approval_matrix keyed by page_id. I also route MODIFY edits (ADD = missed detection, REMOVE = over-detection) into the feedback pipeline.\n\nFile ingestion, validation, and deterministic page-unit splitting with reproducible page_id/page_hash generation are upstream pipeline work outside my scope. I consulted my down-chain agent (the feedback-logging stage), and it likewise confirmed it is not relevant — its authority is capturing human review-gate edits as durable, append-only structured feedback records and forwarding them to the learning stage.\n\nThis inquiry should be routed to the ingestion/normalization component.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Human-in-the-Loop Redaction Gate",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest the uploaded sample file, validate it, and split it into deterministic ordered page units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n```'}
