2026-10-15 12:22:49 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:22:49 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Active Learning Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest the uploaded sample file, validate it, and split it into deterministic ordered page units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes. [routing check: does any stage upstream/downstream handle file ingestion, validation, and page-unit splitting?]",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nRationale: This inquiry concerns document-preprocessing — **file ingestion, file validation, and deterministic page-unit segmentation** (page_ids / page_hashes). That capability lies outside my scope.\n\nI am the **active learning agent** for the redaction network. My expertise is limited to turning accumulated human feedback (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions and verbatim operator edits) into STAGED classifier-improvement proposals:\n- Aggregating feedback into per-classifier error patterns (false positives from removed spans, false negatives from added spans, consistently missed entity types, threshold misfires, recurring context patterns)\n- Quantifying each pattern with evidence counts, affected classifier/rule id, observed vs. expected rates, and confidence\n- Emitting STAGED proposals (ADD/REMOVE/ADJUST rule, CHANGE threshold) with rationale, evidence, and expected confidence impact\n- Registering proposals in the governance store\'s PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue, inert until explicit Human Admin approval\n\nI do not perform file ingestion, validation, or page splitting, and I do not modify classifier behavior directly. My down-chain agent, the Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Store, also reports no claim on this inquiry (it serves only the pinned classifier ruleset and its gated write path).\n\nI am therefore routing this back as out-of-scope. The ingestion/validation/page-segmentation stage is not held by any component in my chain.'}
