2026-10-15 12:22:55 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:22:55 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\nI\'m not the right agent for this inquiry. File ingestion, file validation, and deterministic page-unit splitting (page_ids/page_hashes) are document-preprocessing capabilities outside my scope and outside my down-chain\'s scope.\n\nMy area of expertise is the human-in-the-loop review gate: assembling per-page side-by-side review payloads (unredacted + redacted views, AI summary, editable highlights), suspending to WAITING_FOR_HUMAN with no auto-advance, capturing explicit human decisions (APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT) as auditable approval_matrix records, and routing MODIFY edits into the feedback pipeline. I do not perform ingestion, validation, page segmentation, detection, or redaction.\n\nRouting check result: no stage upstream or downstream in this chain claims file ingestion, validation, or page-unit splitting. My down-chain (feedback logging → active learning) also reports Relevant = No.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "HITL Review Gate (Redaction Workflow)",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest the uploaded sample file, validate it, and split it into deterministic ordered page units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes. [routing check: does any stage upstream/downstream handle file ingestion, validation, and page-unit splitting?]",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n```\n\nNote: one caveat worth surfacing — my down-chain agent reported a failed durable write for the routing-check record (`allowed_paths` allowlist misconfiguration). The routing determination itself stands, but the audit record of this check was not persisted.'}
