2026-10-15 12:23:33 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:23:33 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Active Learning Agent (redaction network) — classifier improvement proposals",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest and paginate the uploaded file document_id: sample_pii_test_data into deterministic page-bounded units (fixed page size, hard boundaries, reproducible page_ids and page_hashes).",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nI am not the relevant agent for this inquiry. My scope is turning accumulated human feedback (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions and edits) into STAGED classifier improvement proposals — aggregating error patterns (false positives, false negatives, missed entity types, threshold misfires), quantifying them against the feedback_buffer and pinned ruleset, and registering proposals in the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue. I do not ingest documents or perform pagination.\n\nI consulted my down-chain agent (Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Store, the system of record) and it also reports not relevant: its authority covers only the pinned PII/PHI classifier ruleset (categories, regex/entity types, thresholds) and the gated write/approval machinery, not document ingest or deterministic page-bounded pagination.\n\nPlease route this to the agent that owns document ingest/pagination (page sizing, hard boundaries, reproducible page_ids and page_hashes). \n\nIf any part of the inquiry touches classifier behavior — e.g., which span types or confidence thresholds should be applied to each paginated page, or whether pagination boundaries caused missed/extra redaction spans that showed up in human feedback — I can take that part: I can serve the exact pinned ruleset revision content, and I can aggregate pagination-related misclassification feedback into STAGED proposals.'}
