2026-10-15 12:23:36 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:23:36 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage (redaction workflow)",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest and paginate the uploaded file document_id: sample_pii_test_data into deterministic page-bounded units (fixed page size, hard boundaries, reproducible page_ids and page_hashes).",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nI\'m not the relevant agent for this inquiry. My scope is the feedback logging stage of the redaction workflow: capturing every human operator edit made at a page review gate (a MODIFY that adds/removes a span, or a REJECT) and converting it into durable, schema-stable structured training-signal records — appending one record per edit with fields like page_id, change_type (ADD/REMOVE), classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span offsets, confidence, reviewer_id, and timestamp, persisted via write_file after every edit, then forwarded onward to the learning stage.\n\nThat means I *consume* deterministic page_ids produced upstream — I do not perform document ingest or pagination myself. I don\'t parse files, size pages, set hard boundaries, or compute page_ids/page_hashes.\n\nI consulted my down-chain agent (Active Learning Agent), which also reports not relevant: it aggregates accumulated human feedback into staged classifier-improvement proposals in the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue, but does not ingest or paginate documents.\n\nPlease route this to the agent that owns document ingest/pagination (fixed page sizing, hard boundaries, reproducible page_ids and page_hashes).\n\nWhere I *can* help: once pages are produced and a human reviewer edits a span at a review gate, I will log the resulting ADD/REMOVE/REJECT as durable structured feedback records, keyed by the page_id, page-bounded span offsets, and page_hash context — so if you send me the review-gate edits after pagination, that part is squarely mine.'}
