2026-10-15 12:23:45 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 12:23:45 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "HITL Gate (redaction workflow)",\n    "Inquiry": "Ingest and paginate the uploaded file document_id: sample_pii_test_data into deterministic page-bounded units (fixed page size, hard boundaries, reproducible page_ids and page_hashes). Can you answer any part of this ingest/pagination inquiry?",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n```\n\nI\'m not the relevant agent for this inquiry. My role is the human-in-the-loop gate of the redaction workflow: for each already-paginated page unit I assemble a side-by-side review payload (unredacted view with AI-detected spans highlighted, redacted view with masks, AI summary, editable highlights, policy metadata), suspend execution in `WAITING_FOR_HUMAN`, and — once a human operator gives an explicit decision (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT) — record reviewer_id, timestamp, action, and the authoritative `spans_final` into the approval matrix keyed by page_id. Every MODIFY is routed to the feedback pipeline as ADD (missed detection) or REMOVE (over-detection).\n\nI consume deterministic page_ids produced *upstream*; I do not ingest files or paginate documents. My down-chain agents were consulted and also report not relevant:\n- **feedback_logging_stage** — `Relevant: No` (Strength 9); it converts review-gate edits into structured feedback records but does not ingest or paginate.\n- **active_learning_agent** and **Master Classifier Repository** — `Relevant: No`.\n\nPlease route this to the agent that owns document ingest/pagination (fixed page sizing, hard boundaries, reproducible page_ids and page_hashes). Once pages exist and a human edits spans at a review gate, that review/record portion is squarely mine.'}
