2026-10-15 13:01:09 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:01:09 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent', 'active_learning_agent'], 'text': 'result from master_classifier_repository_agent\nMy charter is the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset itself: PII/PHI category definitions and hierarchy, per-span regex patterns, recognized named-entity types, and confidence thresholds — served read-only with exact revision identifiers, plus Human-Admin-gated, versioned writes to that ruleset only. Neither named portion of this inquiry (HITL payload assembly/execution control, or operator decision capture into the approval matrix) is owned here; those belong to the HITL payload/execution-control orchestrator and the approval-matrix/feedback-routing owner respectively.\n\nWhere I can add value: if the per-page review payload must cite authoritative span definitions, the payload assembler can request the active pinned ruleset from me and receive the category hierarchy, regex patterns, entity types, thresholds, and the exact pinned revision ID to embed in the payload for auditability.\n\nOne routing caution: operator APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions for a document review must not be submitted through my ruleset write gate. That gate accepts only valid Human Admin approval tokens tied to classifier ruleset revisions; any other submission fails closed and would be misplaced into the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue rather than recorded as a routine review decision in the document approval matrix.\n\nI have no down-chain agents to consult for this routing question, so my determination is based on my own defined scope:\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Master Data Classifiers Ruleset System of Record",\n    "Inquiry": "Present side-by-side HITL review payload per page and capture operator APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions into the approval matrix for the document