ould cite, which is not what was requested.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Master Data Classifiers Ruleset System of Record",\n    "Inquiry": "Human-in-the-loop per-page review payload and approval capture for pages of sample_pii_test_data.txt before final encoding, capturing human operator edit decisions (APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT) and routing MODIFY edits (ADD = missed detection, REMOVE = over-detection) into the feedback pipeline with page_id, reviewer_id, timestamp, and span details.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 8,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "N/A for my scope: per-page review payload capture, operator APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions, and the detection feedback pipeline are owned by the redaction pipeline review/feedback agents, not the classifier ruleset store.",\n        "If any component needs the governing definitions this review would cite (PII/PHI categories, span regexes, named-entity types, confidence thresholds), I can serve the active pinned ruleset read-only with its exact revision identifier.",\n        "If a review outcome is meant to become a change to the classifier definitions, the only path in my scope is a gated write carrying a valid Human Admin approval token; anything else is enqueued as PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
