ange. Once a record is durably persisted I forward accumulated structured feedback onward to the learning stage; I never treat a proposal as approved.",\n        "Clarification needed (multiple agents claim parts of this inquiry): confirm whether the requester wants (a) the review-payload rendering + live APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT capture component (NOT me), (b) the structured logging of MODIFY/REJECT edits into the feedback pipeline with page_id/reviewer_id/timestamp/span (me), (c) aggregation of those logged edits into per-classifier error patterns (down-chain Active Learning Agent), or (d) all of the above. If (d), the inquiry should be split across the review component, me, and the Active Learning Agent.",\n        "Note: the APPROVE decision type is not itself a MODIFY/REJECT edit and carries no span; clarify whether APPROVE events must also be logged as records, since my schema is edit-centric (ADD/REMOVE from MODIFY, or REJECT)."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
