2026-10-15 13:22:15 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:22:15 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent', 'active_learning_agent'], 'text': 'result from master_classifier_repository_agent\nI checked my scope against this inquiry. Here is my determination.\n\nMy stage is the **governed system of record for the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset** — I store, version, and serve the PII/PHI category definitions, regex span patterns, named-entity types, and confidence thresholds that detectors use. I do **not** perform the act of scanning a document and applying redactions to its content; that belongs to the detection/redaction stage downstream of me. I *am* a required dependency for it: redaction of a file must cite and act on the active pinned ruleset revision I serve.\n\n(I attempted to inspect `sample_pii_test_data.txt` directly; access is restricted by the operator-configured allow/block lists, which I cannot influence, so I cannot read the sample here.)\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Governor",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact required information (PII/PHI) from the uploaded file sample_pii_test_data.txt. Determine if this belongs to your stage.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 4,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "The requesting agent must specify which pinned ruleset revision the redaction was performed against so the result can be cited exactly.",\n        "The redaction/detection executor supplies the span types and span boundaries it detected; I supply (read-only) the authoritative PII/PHI category definitions, regex patterns, NER types, and confidence thresholds those detections must conform to.",\n        "Any request to alter, add, or tune the classifier definitions themselves is out of scope for this inquiry and would additionally require a valid Human Admin approval token, failing which it is enqueued as PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW."\n    ]\n}\n```\n\nIn short: the **redaction action itself is not my stage**, but I am the authoritative rules source that redaction must consult — so I am a partial, read-only contributor. I can serve the exact pinned revision of the classifier ruleset on request.'}
