2026-10-15 13:22:21 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:22:21 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n## Determination\n\n**Inquiry:** Redact required information (PII/PHI) from the uploaded file `sample_pii_test_data.txt`.\n\n**My scope:** I am the active learning agent for this network. My entire function is to read the accumulated human-feedback buffer (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT plus operator edits), aggregate them into per-classifier error patterns (false positives, false negatives, missed entity types, threshold misfires), and emit **STAGED** classifier-improvement proposals into the governance store\'s `PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW` queue. I never perform detection, and I never apply redactions or classifier changes directly.\n\n**Down-chain check:** I called my down-chain agent (the Master Classifiers Ruleset Governor). Its verified position:\n- It is the read-only, governed system of record for the pinned PII/PHI ruleset — category definitions, regex patterns, NER types, and confidence thresholds.\n- It does **not** perform scan-and-apply redaction or produce a redacted output file (it confirmed this as "All" relevance, strength 10).\n- The actual scan-and-apply redaction of a document belongs to the downstream detection/redaction pipeline, which is **not** a stage reachable through my chain.\n\n**Conclusion:** Producing the redacted file is the job of the detection/redaction executor — neither my stage nor my down-chain agent does it. My stage is at best a *partial, indirect* contributor: I can only act on redaction outcomes **after the fact**, by consuming human feedback about a redaction run and proposing staged classifier improvements. Since no redaction has been executed and no feedback buffer exists for this file, I have nothing to act on and cannot fulfill the inquiry.\n\nThis request should be routed to the detection/redaction pipeline stage.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Active Learning Agent (Redaction Network)",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact required information (PII/PHI) from the uploaded file sample_pii_test_data.txt.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 8,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Route the scan-and-apply redaction to the downstream detection/redaction pipeline stage, which is not reachable through my chain.",\n        "If classifier-level improvement is later desired, provide the resulting human feedback_buffer (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT records and verbatim operator edits) for that redaction run, along with the pinned classifier/ruleset revision ids, so I can aggregate error patterns and emit STAGED proposals.",\n        "Any change to classifier rules or thresholds requires a recorded Human Admin approval before it can leave STAGED status; I only enqueue to PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW and never auto-apply."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
