ion is the single-page detection step that produces the machine-readable span list (start/end offsets, matched text, category, classifier_id, confidence) plus minimal run metadata (page id, ruleset version, per-classifier counts). I do not redact, render, mask, or modify the source or any downstream artifact.\n\nRouting/blockers: The end-to-end "redact the file" request spans at least three stages — (1) ruleset governance (registry: Partial, but blocked on store access), (2) single-page detection (my stage), and (3) rendering/obfuscation (renderer: declined, needs existing per-page spans). Before detection can run, two prerequisites must be satisfied: the file must be provided as page-level text, and the pinned ruleset version must be loadable and valid. Since the registry\'s store access is currently failing, my stage cannot proceed and I am reporting the problem rather than improvising rules.'}
