paths` list (and confirm `sample_pii_test_data.txt` is inside it), or provide the document as an accessible file path.\n2. Restore `openai_code_interpreter` credentials so I can compute SHA-256 hashes and page_ids deterministically.\n3. Pin the page-boundary policy (e.g., "fixed N-byte pages, split only on the last whole line before N").\n4. Confirm the page_id derivation I intend to use: `page_id = sha256(input_id + ":" + zero-padded index)` where `input_id = sha256(exact full-content bytes)`, and `page_hash = sha256(exact page bytes)`.\n\nNote: content classification/redaction is deliberately out of scope for my stage, so the PII/PHI in this sample is neither my concern nor touched here.\n\n```json\n{\n  "Name": "ingestion_and_pagination_agent",\n  "Inquiry": "Raw text supplied inline for document sample_pii_test_data.txt. Validate type/size, read the exact bytes unmodified, and deterministically chunk into ordered page-bounded units. Return page_units (page_id, page_hash, index, content) and total_pages.",\n  "Mode": "Fulfill",\n  "Response": "Validation of the inline text PASSES on type (.txt accepted), emptiness (non-empty) and size (~3 KB, under the default 1 MB limit), so the input would not be rejected. However, I cannot complete the required read-exact-bytes and deterministic chunk/hash steps: (1) read_file failed with invalid_input: \'allowed_paths\' is required and must be a non-empty list of paths, so exact bytes cannot be read via the tool; (2) openai_code_interpreter failed with Missing credentials, so deterministic page_ids and page_hashes cannot be computed. I am deliberately NOT returning page_units/total_pages, because fabricating hashes or boundaries would violate the idempotency/determinism quality bar. Additionally, no page-boundary policy (fixed byte length vs line-bounded vs form-feed) is configured, which is required for reproducibility. Requirements to proceed: (a) configure read_file allow-list containing the file (or supply an accessible p