2026-10-15 13:26:19 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:26:19 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n**Assessment**\n\nThis inquiry is not my domain, and my down-chain agent (the classifier ruleset store) has confirmed the same.\n\n- The inquiry asks whether the **HITL review gate** can (a) assemble a per-page **side-by-side review payload**, (b) capture a per-page **APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decision**, and (c) route every **MODIFY** edit into the **feedback pipeline**.\n- **Payload assembly and decision capture** belong to the HITL review-gate/orchestration component — not to me and not to the classifier registry.\n- My role is the **active learning agent**: I run on a batch/periodic trigger and *consume* the accumulated `feedback_buffer` to emit **STAGED proposals**. I do **not** assemble review payloads, capture operator decisions, or run the gate. I am a *consumer* of the feedback pipeline, not its capture surface — subsequent in the chain, not the gate itself.\n- My down-chain classifier-registry agent supplies read-only pinned categories/regex/NER/thresholds that a gate would consume, and holds no feedback buffer. So neither of us owns the requested capability.\n\nTwo blocking gaps were also flagged: no raw document text was actually attached inline, and the registry\'s read interface is failing closed, so revision integrity cannot be confirmed.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "ActiveLearningAgent",\n    "Inquiry": "Determine whether the HITL review gate can assemble a per-page side-by-side review payload and capture an operator APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decision for each page, including routing every MODIFY edit into the feedback pipeline.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 8,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Route review-payload assembly and per-page APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT capture to the HITL review-gate/orchestration component, which owns that capability.",\n        "The raw document text for sample_pii_test_data.txt must actually be supplied inline; none was attached, so no paging into page units can occur.",\n        "For the MODIFY-to-feedback-pipeline leg: the gate must write each MODIFY edit into the feedback_buffer I consume; I can only confirm I ingest that buffer, not that the gate routes edits into it.",\n        "Registry read access must be restored so the pinned ruleset revision consumed by the gate can be confirmed."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
