2026-10-15 13:26:42 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:26:42 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage",\n    "Inquiry": "Confirm scope ownership for two legs: (A) per-page side-by-side payload assembly + APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT capture, and (B) routing every MODIFY edit into the feedback pipeline. Also confirm whether the inline raw text was actually attached or is missing, since paging cannot proceed without it.",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "Scope ownership, stated against my actual function:\\n\\n- Leg (B) — routing every MODIFY edit into the feedback pipeline: I am the feedback pipeline\'s *ingestion/logging* stage, so this leg is PARTIALLY mine. My ownership is the receiving end: I take every human operator edit captured at a page review gate (a MODIFY that adds a span, a MODIFY that removes a span, or a REJECT) and convert it into one durable, append-only structured record, persisting via write_file after every edit. I do NOT own the *upstream routing/transport* that carries MODIFY events from the review gate to me — that belongs to the review-gate/capture component. What I can confirm and guarantee: once a MODIFY edit reaches me, it is recorded — never batched, deferred, dropped, deduplicated, or coalesced, even if repeated, near-duplicate, or contradictory across reviewers. One record per edit, schema-stable, machine-readable, with page_id / change_type (ADD or REMOVE) / classifier_id / category / context_snippet / span / confidence / reviewer_id / timestamp; unknown fields explicitly null rather than omitted. My down-chain consumer (Active Learning Agent) confirmed it is NOT the owner of this routing leg — it is strictly downstream, consuming the already-accumulated feedback buffer on a batch/periodic trigger. So the routing leg has no confirmed owner on my chain.\\n\\n- Leg (A) — per-page side-by-side payload assembly + APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT capture: NOT mine. I do not assemble or serve review payloads and hold no state on the capture UI. The Active Learning Agent also returned Not Relevant (Strength 9) for this leg, as did its down-chain (Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Authority). Route leg (A) to the review/payload-assembly owner.\\n\\n- Inline raw text attached vs. missing: I cannot confirm or deny this. I hold no authoritative state on raw-text payload attachment; nothing in my logging scope inspects or asserts attachment status. Route this to whichever component owns raw-text payload attachment.\\n\\nNet: I can own and confirm the *logging/durability* half of leg (B) — every MODIFY edit that reaches me becomes a persisted record forwarded onward to the learning stage. I cannot confirm ownership of the routing/transport half of (B), leg (A), or the attachment status, and no downstream agent on my chain claims them either."\n}'}
