category hierarchy, per-span regex patterns, recognized NER entity types, and the confidence thresholds that determine when a span is flagged sensitive. That ruleset is exactly what a redaction pipeline needs to cover the listed PII (names, DOB, SSN, phone, email, address, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN) and PHI (medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription) categories.\n\nWhat I do **not** own: executing the redaction, and the ingestion/pagination decision — those are pipeline/orchestration concerns handled by other agents. Also, no write to the ruleset is possible from this inquiry, since it carries no valid Human Admin approval token; any proposed change would be queued as PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW and exposed for inspection rather than applied.'}
