2026-10-15 13:37:46 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:37:46 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent', 'active_learning_agent'], 'text': 'result from master_classifier_repository_agent\nI am the governed system of record for the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset. The actual act of redacting an uploaded document — and the question of whether ingestion/pagination applies to that document — sits with the redaction/ingestion pipeline, not with me. My contribution is narrower and only indirectly relevant: I am the sole authority that stores and serves the classifier definitions (PII/PHI categories, regex patterns, NER types, confidence thresholds) that such a redaction run must cite.\n\nI could not read the ruleset store to serve a pinned revision (the store call was rejected: `allowed_paths` config missing), so I cannot yet return a concrete revision identifier for this inquiry.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Store",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact relevant sensitive information from an uploaded document: a customer support & DSAR request log test dataset containing customer PII (names, DOB, SSN, phones, email, addresses, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN) and health information (medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription). Determine if ingestion/pagination applies.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 4,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "The redaction/detection engine agent (owner of span detection and document redaction) must fulfill the core request; this is outside the ruleset store\'s scope.",\n        "The ingestion/pagination decision belongs to the document-ingestion owner, not the ruleset store; it must be routed there.",\n        "From the ruleset store, the pipeline must obtain the active PINNED ruleset revision so all span categories (PII: names, DOB, SSN, phone, email, address, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN; PHI: medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription), their regex/NER definitions, and the governing confidence thresholds are cited to an exact revision identifier.",\n        "Provide a valid read path / access to the ruleset store so the exact pinned revision identifier and content can be served; the current store call was rejected (missing allowed_paths configuration)."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
