2026-10-15 13:38:40 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:38:40 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Active Learning Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Determine whether the HITL review gateway applies to the redaction of the customer support & DSAR request log test dataset, and if so, what the logging stage requires from the gateway to log edits.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 4,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Confirm which component owns the dataset-scoping decision for the HITL review gateway (I do not own gateway applicability).",\n        "Confirm which component owns the gateway-to-logging interface contract; I only specify what the downstream learning stage consumes, not what the gateway must emit."\n    ],\n    "Notes": {\n        "Can answer": "Only the downstream-consumer slice: what the learning stage requires to exist in the logged feedback_buffer for me to be able to aggregate error patterns. Specifically I require each logged human decision to be captured in a structured form (APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT), preserve operator edits VERBATIM (no paraphrase), carry the affected span/classifier-rule reference, and retain dataset identifier so records are traceable to the customer support & DSAR request log test dataset. Without dataset-level tagging, I cannot attribute error patterns to this dataset.",\n        "Cannot answer": "Whether the HITL review gateway applies to this dataset at all (dataset-scoping/eligibility is not a learning-stage decision), and the full set of logging-stage requirements the gateway must satisfy to emit edits (that is the gateway\'s and the logging component\'s contract)."\n    }\n}'}
