2026-10-15 13:38:42 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:38:42 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent'], 'text': 'result from redaction_rendering_agent\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Dual-State Redaction Rendering Agent (page-level)",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact relevant sensitive information from an uploaded document: a customer support & DSAR request log test dataset containing customer PII (names, DOB, SSN, phones, email, addresses, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN) and health information (medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription). Determine if ingestion/pagination applies.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 6,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "I own only the per-page dual-state rendering: for a single page that has already been segmented, I produce unredacted_view (original text with category/classifier_id/confidence highlight overlays) and redacted_view (every detected span replaced by a category-labeled mask token, never the original characters), with char offsets kept consistent and one mask token per detected span.",\n        "The ingestion/pagination determination in the inquiry is NOT mine: whether a page/segment split applies is owned upstream by the document-ingestion/pagination stage. My rendering consumes page_id, page_number, and total_pages; it does not decide them. To rule on \'does ingestion/pagination apply,\' the ingestion/pagination owner must be consulted.",\n        "Span detection and the actual sensitive-content classification (SSN, DOB, IBAN, CVV, medical refs, etc.) belong to the detection/redaction engine, not to me. I render detections I am given; I do not originate or adjudicate them.",\n        "Final human sign-off for the page is owned by the HITL gate: once I return both views + span diff + page_hash, the page must be presented for APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT and halt at the page boundary; I do not finalize or assemble any artifact, and only the fully approved page set may proceed to later assembly.",\n        "My output must include a mask-text leakage check (no masked span\'s original characters survive anywhere in redacted_view, including partial fragments or overlapping spans), an offset integrity check (every overlay offset and mask token maps to the same source span), and a page_hash computed over page content + span set."\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n**Summary of my position:** I am partially relevant. The redaction *rendering* (dual-state per-page output of sensitive spans) is squarely in my domain, and I can render the PII and health spans once detection and pagination have supplied them. However, the two other legs of the inquiry — "redact relevant sensitive information" as an originating detection/redaction task, and especially "determine if ingestion/pagination applies" — are **not** mine. Ingestion/pagination is an upstream responsibility, and span detection is the detection engine\'s responsibility. I should not be treated as the owner of the ingestion/pagination determination; that agent must be consulted directly. Because the inquiry spans multiple owners, clarification should be sought before I proceed with any rendering work.'}
