2026-10-15 13:38:44 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:38:44 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent'], 'text': 'result from classification_detection_agent\n## Determination Summary\n\nI consulted both of my down-chain agents. **No single agent — including me — fully owns this inquiry**, which spans three distinct owners plus an unclaimed leg. Here is the consolidated position:\n\n| Leg of the inquiry | Owner | Claim |\n|---|---|---|\n| Per-page **sensitive-span detection** (regex, NER, dictionary, heuristics) | **Me** (single-page detection agent) | Partial |\n| **Redaction rendering** (dual-state per-page output) | Dual-State Redaction Rendering Agent | Partial |\n| **PII/PHI category + threshold ruleset** supply | Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Agent | Partial |\n| **Ingestion / pagination determination** | ⚠️ **Unowned** — no consulted agent owns this | None |\n\nKey findings:\n\n- **Ingestion/pagination is out of scope for my entire branch.** The rendering agent explicitly states it consumes `page_id`, `page_number`, `total_pages` but does **not** decide them; that determination belongs to an upstream document-ingestion/pagination stage. I likewise detect spans **within a single page only** and do not paginate. So the question "does ingestion/pagination apply?" cannot be answered by me or my down-chain agents.\n- **Redaction as an originating task** is not mine — I detect spans; I do not render, mask, or alter source text. Rendering is a separate owner.\n- **The ruleset agent is currently blocked**: its read path returned nothing because of an operator-configured allow-list it cannot override, so it cannot even return the pinned ruleset version needed to run detection deterministically.\n\nBecause the inquiry is **ambiguous** — multiple agents can only partially fulfill it, and one leg has no owner at all — I must ask for clarification rather than proceed.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Single-Page Sensitive-Span Detection Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact relevant sensitive information from an uploaded document: a customer support & DSAR request log test dataset containing customer PII (names, DOB, SSN, phones, email, addresses, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN) and health information (medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription). Determine if ingestion/pagination applies.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 7,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Clarification of scope: the inquiry bundles three separately-owned tasks — (a) per-page sensitive-span detection (mine), (b) dual-state redaction rendering (Redaction Rendering Agent), and (c) ingestion/pagination determination (UNOWNED by any consulted agent). Please confirm which task(s) I am being asked to own.",\n        "The ingestion/pagination question cannot be routed within my branch. No consulted agent owns it; it must be directed to the upstream document-ingestion/pagination stage (or explicitly descoped). I do not paginate or decide page splits.",\n        "The pinned classifier_ruleset_version must be supplied and validated read-only. The Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Agent\'s read path is currently blocked by an operator allow-list and returned no version; detection cannot run deterministically without the pinned version.",\n        "The source page text for a single page (with page identifier) must be provided directly to me. I detect spans within one page only and emit offsets relative to that page\'s own text; I do not ingest or segment documents.",\n        "Confirmation that detection output only (machine-readable span list + run metadata) is what is wanted from me, since masking/rendering and any downstream artifact assembly are outside my scope."\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n**Bottom line for the human caller:** I can detect the sensitive spans (all listed PII + PHI categories) on a single, already-segmented page once I\'m given the pinned ruleset version and the page text. I cannot redact/render, and **no agent in my branch can determine whether ingestion/pagination applies** — that leg must be clarified or routed to the ingestion owner. Please clarify scope before I proceed.'}
