2026-10-15 13:38:50 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:38:50 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent'], 'text': 'result from ingestion_pagination_agent\n## Determination Summary\n\nThe inquiry bundles three separately-owned legs, and I own exactly one of them — the leg that was flagged as unowned by my peer\'s branch.\n\n| Leg of the inquiry | Owner | Claim |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Ingestion + deterministic pagination** → ordered `page_units` (page_id, page_hash, index, content) + `total_pages` | **Me** (Ingestion & Pagination stage) | Partial |\n| Per-page sensitive-span detection | Single-Page Sensitive-Span Detection Agent | Partial |\n| Dual-state redaction rendering | Redaction Rendering Agent | Partial |\n| Category/threshold ruleset supply | Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Agent | Partial |\n\n**Answer to "Does ingestion/pagination apply?": Yes.** This inquiry cannot proceed through the pipeline without it. Every downstream stage consumes `page_id`, `index`/page_number, and `total_pages` but none of them *decide* page boundaries — that is precisely my stage. So ingestion/pagination applies as the **prerequisite step**, and it is the one leg no other agent can cover.\n\n**What I can own here (partial):**\n- Validate the uploaded input (.txt/.md/.csv or raw stream), rejecting unsupported type, empty content, oversize, or encoding failure with a precise reason.\n- Read raw content byte-exact via `read_file` (extracting the `content` string if the tool returns structured output), with no normalization/trim/re-encode.\n- Produce deterministic, reproducible page-bounded `page_units` — stable page_ids derived from input identity + index, page_hashes over exact page bytes — plus `total_pages`, in original order with no gaps/overlaps.\n\n**What I cannot own:** redaction itself, span detection, ruleset supply, and artifact assembly. Those stay with their owners.\n\n**Ambiguity flag:** the inquiry is phrased as "redact… and determine if ingestion/pagination applies" — if the human only wants the *determination*, I can answer directly (Yes). If they want me to actually **produce the page_units**, I need the input and must not be asked to modify content, since my output must be byte-for-byte identical to the source.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Ingestion & Pagination Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact relevant sensitive information from an uploaded document: a customer support & DSAR request log test dataset containing customer PII (names, DOB, SSN, phones, email, addresses, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN) and health information (medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription). Determine if ingestion/pagination applies.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "The ingestion/pagination leg is mine and it DOES apply: it is the upstream prerequisite that all detection/rendering stages depend on (they consume page_id/page_number/total_pages but do not decide them). Please confirm the human wants me to own this leg.",\n        "Direct answer to the literal question: Yes, ingestion/pagination applies. If only the determination is wanted, no further input is needed.",\n        "To actually perform it, the uploaded document path (or raw text stream) must be provided, restricted to .txt/.md/.csv; otherwise I will flag unsupported-type / empty / oversize / encoding-failure and stop.",\n        "Clarification of scope: the inquiry bundles three tasks. I own ingestion + deterministic pagination only; sensitive-span detection, redaction rendering, ruleset supply, and artifact assembly are owned elsewhere and must be routed separately.",\n        "Constraint acknowledgment: my output stays byte-for-byte unmodified — I will not redact, sanitize, or normalize content. Redaction is out of my scope.",\n        "A deterministic identity source (e.g., input path/hash) is needed so page_ids and page_hashes are reproducible across idempotent re-runs; no timestamps, randomness, or non-deterministic ordering will be introduced."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
