2026-10-15 13:38:50 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:38:50 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\nAs the HITL review gateway component, this inquiry falls directly within my area of expertise. My down-chain logging agent confirmed it cannot own the gateway-scoping decision (its relevance is Partial and strictly event-based, downstream of the gate), so I own this determination.\n\n**Applicability determination:** Yes — the HITL review gateway applies. This is a test dataset containing customer PII and health information (PHI), i.e., high-sensitivity categories. Per policy, sensitive-data redaction pages are human-reviewed one page at a time via side-by-side review payloads, with execution suspended to WAITING_FOR_HUMAN and no auto-advance. The gateway applies to this dataset exactly as it would to production pages; nothing about "test dataset" status exempts it.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "HITL Review Gateway (Redaction Workflow)",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact relevant sensitive information from an uploaded document: a customer support & DSAR request log test dataset containing customer PII and health information. Determine if the HITL review gateway applies.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "I own gateway applicability and the human review gate only. I do NOT perform detection, redaction, or learning — those sit with the redaction decisioning/detection stage and the Master Data Classifiers Ruleset store (entity-category/subtype definitions and span thresholds).",\n        "Applicability = YES: this dataset contains PII and health information (high-sensitivity). Each page unit is presented as a deterministic side-by-side review payload (page_id, page_number, total_pages; unredacted_view with AI-detected spans highlighted; redacted_view with masks; ai_summary; actions APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT; editable_highlights; policy_metadata.auto_advance_on_timeout=false). Execution then halts in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN.",\n        "No auto-advance on timeout: if no human decision arrives, the gate remains WAITING_FOR_HUMAN and surfaces that state — approval is never fabricated, inferred, or defaulted.",\n        "On decision I record reviewer_id, timestamp, chosen action, and spans_final (authoritative post-edit span set) into the approval_matrix keyed by page_id.",\n        "Every MODIFY edit is routed to the feedback pipeline: ADD = missed detection/false negative, REMOVE = over-detection/false positive, preserving page_id, reviewer_id, timestamp, and span details. My down-chain logging agent requires, per edit: page_id (dataset-attributable), change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp — forwarded immediately, append-only, no dedupe/coalescing, null for unknown fields."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
