antees no gaps/overlaps; final window may be short).\n4. For index `i` (0-based): `page_id = f"{doc_id}-p{i:04d}"`, `page_hash = sha256(window.encode(\'utf-8\')).hexdigest()`.\n5. Verify `\'\'.join(pages) == content`.\n6. Emit ordered `page_units` (`index`, `page_id`, `page_hash`, `content`) + `total_pages`.\n\nNo `page_units`, `total_pages`, or hashes are returned yet, precisely because the reproducibility guarantee cannot be met at this moment.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Ingestion & Pagination Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "ingest and deterministically paginate the following uploaded document into ordered page-bounded units with reproducible page_ids/page_hashes and total_pages. Document identity: inline test dataset \\"CUSTOMER SUPPORT & DSAR REQUEST LOGS - TEST DATASET\\".",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "BLOCKED. Ingestion and input validation succeeded: input is a non-empty inline raw-text/plaintext document within the size limit, accepted and read verbatim with no character/whitespace/line-ending alteration. However, the deterministic page-bounded chunking step could not be performed because the openai_code_interpreter tool is unavailable (error: \'Missing credentials. Please pass an api_key... or set OPENAI_API_KEY\'). Deterministic pagination requires SHA-256 digests for page_hash and a hash-derived doc_id for page_id, which cannot be computed reliably without the execution tool; fabricating hashes would violate the idempotent/byte-exact quality bar, so none were emitted. ACTIONABLE FLAG: restore code-execution credentials, then re-run the pinned recipe: content verbatim; doc_id=sha256(content)[:16]; windows of CHUNK=1000 chars, stride=CHUNK, last window may be shorter; page_id=f\'{doc_id}-p{i:04d}\'; page_hash=sha256(window); verify join(pages)==content; emit ordered page_units (index, page_id, page_hash, content) + total_pages. Down-chain agents (Sensitive Span Detection and its sub-agents) confirmed they are not relevant to ingestion/pagination."\n}\n```'}
