2026-10-15 13:52:41 BST | INFO     | NeuroSan:_log:821 - NeuroSan - {"message": "Received a agent_network_designer.StreamingChat request for 'design and create a network for - ### CORE OPERATING WORKFLOW & REQUIREMENTS 1. TEXT FILE INGESTION - Accept uploaded text files (.txt, .md, raw text streams). - Validate input format, size, and encoding before initializing the pipeline state. 2. MASTER CLASSIFICATION REPOSITORY (GOVERNANCE) - Maintain a centralized repository of data classifiers (regex patterns, entity types, categories) that dictate what gets redacted and what passes through. - The AI agent network may analyze edge cases and PROPOSE classifier updates, additions, or modifications. - MANDATORY GOVERNANCE GATE: No repository rule or classifier can be added, edited, or removed without explicit, authenticated Human Admin approval. 3. HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP REDACTION APPROVAL - Process text and apply proposed redactions using the master classifier rules. - Present the proposed redactions for Human Operator review. - STRICT GATES: The system MUST NOT proceed, render, or finalize any document until the human explicitly reviews and approves all redaction actions. Support operator modifications (adding/removing redaction spans) on the fly. 4. IRREVERSIBLE OBFUSCATION & FINAL ENCODING - Upon receiving full human approval for the document's redactions, trigger the hardening engine. - Assemble a brand-new obfuscated file that strips all source metadata, underlying text layers, and revision history. - Ensure the final output is completely irreversible—it cannot be un-edited, reversed, or mapped back to the original source text. 5. CONTINUOUS ACTIVE LEARNING - Log every human decision, approval, and rejection (including manual span additions or false-positive removals). - Route these decision logs into an active learning buffer. - Periodically aggregate feedback patterns to generate fine-tuned, evidence-backed classifier suggestions for future human admin review.'", "user_id":