2026-10-15 13:53:49 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:53:49 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer'], 'text': "Structure created. Now I'll generate the agent instructions and descriptions."}
2026-10-15 13:53:49 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 13:53:49 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer'], 'text': 'Invoking: `__agent_network_instructions_editor` with:\n{"invoking_start": true, "invoked_agent_name": "__agent_network_instructions_editor", "params": {"agent_network_description": "Create detailed instructions and descriptions for all agents in the RedactionPipeline network, enforcing the five-stage workflow and all mandatory human gates.\\n\\nAgents and required responsibilities:\\n\\n1. Ingestion & Validation Agent (entry point)\\n   - Accept uploaded text files (.txt, .md, raw text streams).\\n   - Validate input format, size, and encoding. Reject unsupported formats/oversized/undecodable files with a clear error.\\n   - Initialize and own the pipeline state for each document; pass validated text downstream to the Redaction Proposal Agent and notify the Classifier Repository/Governance Agent that a new document is in scope.\\n   - Use read_file to read uploaded file content.\\n\\n2. Classifier Repository / Governance Agent\\n   - Own and maintain the centralized master classifier repository (regex patterns, entity types, categories) that dictates what is redacted vs. passed through.\\n   - Supply the current active rule set to the Redaction Proposal Agent.\\n   - Analyze edge cases surfaced from review and PROPOSE classifier additions/modifications/removals.\\n   - Enforce the MANDATORY GOVERNANCE GATE: never commit any rule change without explicit, authenticated Human Admin approval obtained through the HITL subnetwork. Present proposals to the Human Admin and only apply changes after authenticated approval is received and recorded.\\n   - Receive evidence-backed suggestions from the Active Learning Agent and route them to the Human Admin for review.\\n\\n3. Redaction Proposal Agent\\n   - Apply the master classifier rules to validated text and generate proposed redaction spans (with span locations, matched classifier, and rationale).\\n   - Support operator modifications: adding new redaction spans and removing false-positive spans on the fly; re-evaluate affected spans when rules or manual edits change.\\n   - Do NOT finalize; hand all proposals to the Human Review Gate Coordinator. Use openai_code_interpreter for span computation/regex evaluation.\\n\\n4. Human Review Gate Coordinator Agent\\n   - Present every proposed redaction to the Human Operator for review via the HITL subnetwork.\\n   - Enforce the STRICT GATE: the system MUST NOT proceed, render, or finalize any document until the human explicitly reviews and approves all redaction actions. Block downstream flow otherwise.\\n   - Capture operator decisions (approvals, rejections, manual additions, false-positive removals) and pass full decision logs to the Active Learning Agent.\\n   - Only after full approval, release the document to the Obfuscation/Hardening Engine Agent.\\n\\n5. Obfuscation / Hardening Engine Agent\\n   - Trigger ONLY upon verified full human approval from the Human Review Gate Coordinator. Never run without it.\\n   - Assemble a brand-new obfuscated file that strips all source metadata, underlying text layers, and revision history.\\n   - Ensure output is completely irreversible \\u2014 cannot be un-edited, reversed, or mapped back to the original text.\\n   - Write the final irreversible output using write_file.\\n\\n6. Active Learning Agent\\n   - Log every human decision, approval, rejection, manual span addition, and false-positive removal into an active learning buffer.\\n   - Periodically aggregate feedback patterns and generate fine-tuned, evidence-backed classifier suggestions.\\n   - Route suggestions to the Classifier Repository/Governance Agent for (proposed) human admin review.\\n\\nEmphasize as safety invariants throughout: no rule change without authenticated Human Admin approval; no document finalization without full Human Operator approval; irreversible output only after approval.", "mode": "create"}}'}
