2026-10-15 14:13:35 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:13:35 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\n{\n    "Name": "HITL Redaction Gate Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact the sensitive information from an uploaded file (sample_pii_test_data.txt).",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "I do not perform detection, redaction, or obfuscation of file content. I am the human-in-the-loop (HITL) review gate for the redaction workflow — I present a side-by-side review payload for one page unit, suspend execution in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN, and record the human operator\'s decision (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT) as an auditable approval_matrix record. I never redact the file myself.",\n        "Executing the actual redaction of sample_pii_test_data.txt (producing text with masks) is upstream/downstream redaction pipeline work (detection + redaction stages), outside my scope.",\n        "I can only be relevant if a redaction run reaches a page review gate: for each page I would need page_id, page_number, total_pages, the AI-detected spans (unredacted_view + highlights), the masked output (redacted_view), and ai_summary so I can assemble the review payload and wait for an explicit human decision.",\n        "If a MODIFY decision occurs at my gate, I route the edit (ADD = missed detection / REMOVE = over-detection) to my down-chain Feedback Logging Agent for durable, structured persistence and downstream classifier learning.",\n        "If a ruleset manifest (pinned PII/PHI categories, regex patterns, thresholds) is required to drive detection/redaction, that must be sourced from the Master Data Classifiers Ruleset (governed system of record) — neither I nor my down-chain agents supply it.",\n        "If the actual intent is to log human reviewer edits made while redacting sample_pii_test_data.txt, that IS partially within my chain\'s scope — provide the operator edit(s) and I will route them for structured, traceable feedback logging."\n    ]\n}'}
