sion (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT). This path is rejected.\n\n**3. Pinned ruleset version missing.**\n`classifier_ruleset_version` is unset. The upstream ruleset authority is unreachable (store-path / `allowed_paths` access error). I pin one ruleset version for the entire document and never change it mid-document — without it, detection and redaction cannot lawfully run.\n\n### What this means for your request\nI cannot deliver a redacted artifact for this file right now. The upstream detection stage cannot be trusted with this document until the integrity failure is resolved, and no human operator has reviewed any page. Redaction ≠ auto-accept; it must pass the gate.\n\n### What I can do the moment these clear\n- **Ingest & paginate** deterministically into ordered `page_units` with reproducible `page_id`/`page_hash` once the file is readable at a resolvable path.\n- **Route page-by-page** through the Human-in-the-Loop review gate, holding one page in flight at a time, and record each operator verdict with reviewer_id + timestamp.\n- **Enforce the completion gate**: assemble, harden, and independently verify the artifact only after 100% approval coverage.\n\n### To unblock, please provide\n1. **Confirmation of the correct source document / access to `sample_pii_test_data.txt`** at a resolvable path — and a re-run of detection against the *actual* content (the current span set does not match it).\n2. **The pinned `classifier_ruleset_version`** (or resolution of the ruleset store-path access error).\n3. **Human operator availability** for per-page APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT — the gate will not auto-advance and will not time out into approval.\n\nAll of the above is captured in the append-only audit log. Confirm items 1–3 and I will sequence the pipeline and report back at each page boundary."}
