2026-10-15 14:25:07 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:25:07 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\nYour role confirmation is squarely within my scope. Here is my determination.\n\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage (redaction workflow)",\n    "Inquiry": "A document (/Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt) is entering the pipeline for initial discovery/redaction. Confirm your role for capturing human operator edits (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT) from page review gates into structured, append-only feedback records containing page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, and timestamp, forwarded for downstream classifier learning.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 10,\n    "Claim": "All",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "I capture every human operator edit emitted at a page review gate: MODIFY that adds a span the classifier missed (change_type = ADD) or removes/rejects a classifier-flagged span (change_type = REMOVE), and REJECT events. Note on field naming: the pipeline speaks of APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT, while the durable record schema expresses change_type as ADD/REMOVE — each edit maps to exactly one record, with APPROVE-only page gates producing no span edit record.",\n        "One structured record per edit, emitted with the exact fields: page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp. Genuinely unknown values are recorded explicitly as null/unknown rather than omitted.",\n        "Records are append-only and durable: persisted immediately via write_file after every edit (no batching, deferral, or in-memory holding), never overwritten, mutated, deleted, deduplicated, or coalesced — including repeated, near-duplicate, or contradictory edits from the same or different reviewers.",\n        "Edits are preserved exactly as made; reviewer intent is not normalized away.",\n        "On write failure I report the failure explicitly and retry; success is never reported unless the record is confirmed persisted.",\n        "Downstream: I forward the accumulated structured feedback to the Active Learning Agent for classifier learning. Per confirmation from that agent (Strength 9, Claim All), it requires the records as structured, append-only entries with the full field set and consumes context_snippet/span verbatim; it aggregates feedback into staged proposals registered in the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue and never auto-applies classifier updates. Note: runtime redaction of the document itself is NOT my function — I only log and forward feedback.",\n        "Open items routed downstream: confirmation of which workflow half is being routed (raw feedback-record ingestion vs. registration of staged proposals), and confirmation of the active pinned ruleset revision identifier to diff proposals against."\n    ]\n}'}
