ce of truth for downstream rendering.",\n        "MODIFY routing: every MODIFY edit is routed to the feedback pipeline — ADD = missed detection (false negative), REMOVE = over-detection (false positive) — preserving page_id, reviewer_id, timestamp, and span details.",\n        "Confirmed down-chain: the Feedback Logging Stage (Relevant: Yes, Strength 10, Claim All) captures every edit into append-only, durable, one-record-per-edit feedback records with fields page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp, and forwards them to the Active Learning Agent for classifier learning.",\n        "Boundary note: runtime detection, redaction, and classifier learning are NOT my function; I present payloads, gate on human decision, and record outcomes. Detection/redaction semantics belong to the discovery/redaction stages."\n    ]\n}\n```\n\nSummary: Yes — I confirm both roles. I prepare the per-page side-by-side review payloads, suspend at WAITING_FOR_HUMAN, and record explicit human APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions (reviewer_id, timestamp, spans_final) into the approval_matrix keyed by page_id. I do not auto-advance on timeout and never fabricate or default an approval. MODIFY edits flow through the Feedback Logging Stage into the learning pipeline.'}
