2026-10-15 14:56:17 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:56:16 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\n{\n    "Name": "feedback_logging_agent",\n    "Inquiry": "A file is uploaded at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt - validate the document type/size, read its raw content unmodified, and deterministically chunk it into ordered page-bounded units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes. Emit page_units and total_pages, and flag if malformed or unsupported.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nI\'m not relevant to this inquiry. My role is the feedback logging stage of the redaction workflow: I capture human operator edits made at page review gates (ADD/REMOVE span edits and REJECTs) and convert them into durable, structured training-signal records (page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp), persisting each append-only via write_file and forwarding accumulated records to the learning stage.\n\nDocument ingestion tasks — validating document type/size, reading raw content, chunking into page-bounded units with page_ids/page_hashes, and emitting page_units/total_pages — fall outside my scope. I do not perform file validation, reading, or chunking, and I don\'t decide/approve/apply classifier changes. If you have a human operator edit at a review gate to log, I can handle that.'}
