2026-10-15 14:56:19 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:56:19 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\nI\'m not relevant to this inquiry.\n\nMy scope is strictly the human-in-the-loop (HITL) review gate for the redaction workflow — I take already-chunked **page units**, present a side-by-side review payload (unredacted view with highlights vs. redacted masked view plus an AI summary), halt execution in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN, and capture the human operator\'s decision (APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT) as an auditable approval_matrix record keyed by page_id.\n\nWhat this inquiry asks for is upstream **document ingestion / preprocessing** — validating the file\'s type and size, reading raw content unmodified, deterministically chunking it into ordered page-bounded units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes, emitting page_units and total_pages, and flagging malformed/unsupported inputs. That is not something I do, and my down-chain feedback logging agent also confirmed it is out of scope (it only handles operator edit capture at review gates).\n\nI can help once you have `page_units` — specifically, presenting each page for review, holding for an explicit human decision with no auto-advance on timeout, recording the decision, and routing any MODIFY edits (ADD = missed detection, REMOVE = over-detection) into the feedback pipeline.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "hitl_gate",\n    "Inquiry": "A file is uploaded at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt - validate the document type/size, read its raw content unmodified, and deterministically chunk it into ordered page-bounded units with reproducible page_ids and page_hashes. Emit page_units and total_pages, and flag if malformed or unsupported.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n```'}
