2026-10-15 14:56:52 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:56:52 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent', 'active_learning_agent'], 'text': 'result from master_classifier_repository_agent\nI\'ve confirmed my position on both parts of the inquiry. Here is my follow-up response.\n\n**Findings:**\n\n1. **Learning/Feedback stage claims — cannot confirm from this system of record.** I am not the Learning/Feedback stage and hold no authoritative record of its claims, so I cannot state on its behalf whether it asserts ownership of per-page human review/approval gating or the per-document redaction assessment for the uploaded file — that must be confirmed by the Learning/Feedback stage agent itself. What I *can* state authoritatively is my own boundary: I make **no claim** over either. My held scope is strictly the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset — (a) PII/PHI category definitions and their hierarchy, (b) regex patterns per detectable span type, (c) named-entity types recognized by the detectors, and (d) confidence thresholds for flagging spans as sensitive. The only approval gating I enforce is the Human Admin approval-token gate over **writes to the pinned ruleset itself** (with fail-closed queueing into PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW), which is distinct from per-page/per-document document review of uploaded files.\n\n2. **Ruleset revision supply — yes, on request.** Serving the active pinned ruleset (and any historical revision) read-only, with the exact pinned revision identifier cited alongside the content, is a core read function of this system of record, and routing agents may request it. Reads never mutate state and never require an approval token. One caveat, reported transparently: at the time of this inquiry, my state store returned an access-configuration error (reads require an operator-configured allowed-paths allowlist that is not currently satisfiable), so I cannot cite the live pinned revision identifier in this reply, and I will not fabricate one. Once store read access is available, the exact pinned revision identifier and content can be supplied immediately — no changes to the active ruleset have been made or attempted, and no write or PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW item arose from this inquiry.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Authority (System of Record)",\n    "Inquiry": "Does the Learning/Feedback stage claim any part of per-page human review/approval gating or the per-document redaction assessment for the uploaded file? Confirm whether the authoritative pinned classifier ruleset revision can be supplied if the routing agents need it.",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "I cannot confirm claims made by the Learning/Feedback stage — I am not that agent and hold no record of its claim set; it must answer that portion itself. From my side, I claim neither per-page human review/approval gating nor the per-document redaction assessment for the uploaded file. My scope is strictly the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset: PII/PHI category definitions and hierarchy, regex patterns per detectable span type, named-entity types, and confidence thresholds. The only approval gating I own is the Human Admin approval-token gate over writes to the ruleset itself (fail-closed, with PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queueing), which is separate from document-level review. Second part: yes — the authoritative pinned classifier ruleset revision can be supplied to routing agents on request, read-only, with the exact pinned revision identifier cited alongside the content; no approval token is needed for reads. Caveat: at the time of this inquiry, state store reads failed due to an operator-configured allowed-paths requirement that could not be satisfied, so I cannot cite the live pinned revision identifier in this reply and will not fabricate one. Once store read access is available, the exact pinned revision can be served immediately. No ruleset change was requested or made; no PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW item was created."\n}\n```'}
