the Human Admin approval gate over *ruleset writes*. It can supply the authoritative pinned ruleset revision read-only to whichever agent needs it, but flagged it could not read its state store during this inquiry and would not fabricate a revision identifier.\n\n**Routing suggestion:** the two functions named belong to the **document redaction assessment agent** and the **per-page HITL approval-gating agent**, neither of which is in my chain.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Active Learning Agent (redaction network)",\n    "Inquiry": "A file is uploaded at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt - assess for redaction. Are you the correct agent to handle the per-page human review/approval gating for this document? (Forwarded for Determine: routing clarification within the HITL redaction pipeline - I am the feedback-logging stage and am checking whether the learning stage claims any part of the per-page review/approval gating or the redaction assessment itself.)",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Route per-document redaction assessment to the document assessment/detector agent that consumes the pinned classifier ruleset.",\n        "Route per-page human review/approval gating to the HITL approval-gating agent that owns page-level human sign-off.",\n        "No requirement from me for these two functions; the Learning/Feedback stage claims no part of either. I become relevant only downstream, when structured human APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions and span edits are accumulated for classifier-improvement proposal generation."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
