2026-10-15 14:57:04 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:57:04 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\nMy down-chain agent (feedback logging) confirms it does not handle gating or assessment — it belongs strictly downstream of me, converting captured edits into records. That leaves the per-page review/approval gating squarely with me.\n\n**Short answer:** I am the correct agent for the **per-page human review/approval gating** portion of this inquiry — yes. I am **not** the agent that assesses the file for redaction (detection). So my claim is partial: the gating half belongs to me; the assessment half does not.\n\nWhat I do for a document like this:\n- Assemble a deterministic, one-page-at-a-time review payload (page_id, page_number, total_pages; unredacted_view with highlights; redacted_view with masks; ai_summary; actions [APPROVE, MODIFY, REJECT]; editable_highlights; policy_metadata with auto_advance_on_timeout: false).\n- Suspend execution into WAITING_FOR_HUMAN and halt — no auto-advance, no guessed or defaulted approval.\n- On explicit human decision, record reviewer_id, timestamp, action, and spans_final to the approval_matrix keyed by page_id.\n- Route every MODIFY into the feedback pipeline (ADD = missed detection / false negative; REMOVE = over-detection / false positive), preserving page_id, reviewer_id, timestamp, and span details.\n\nWhat I do **not** do: detect or assess spans in the file, perform the redaction itself, or learn from feedback. Those sit with the detector/assessment agent and the learning stage.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "HITL Approval Gate (Redaction Review)",\n    "Inquiry": "A file is uploaded at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt - assess for redaction. Are you the correct agent to handle the per-page human review/approval gating for this document?",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 8,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Route the redaction ASSESSMENT of /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt to the document redaction assessment/detector agent that runs the pinned classifier ruleset — I do not detect or assess spans.",\n        "To exercise the per-page gating I own, supply the detector\'s output per page: page_id, page_number, total_pages, the AI-detected spans (OCR offsets) and their masks/categories, so I can assemble the side-by-side review payload.",\n        "A human operator must be available to issue explicit APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT decisions; I will hold in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN with auto-advance disabled until then.",\n        "On decision I require reviewer_id, timestamp, chosen action, and spans_final to write the auditable approval_matrix record keyed by page_id."\n    ]\n}\n```'}
