ible: page-bounded chunking → per-page detection/redaction → human review gate per page → final hardening → completion.\n- The span **detection/redaction assessment** step is performed by the upstream redaction/detector stage (which runs the pinned classifier ruleset), not by the gating or hardening stages.\n\n### To unblock — choose one\n1. **Fix the allow-list:** Populate the operator's `allowed_paths` to include `data/` or the specific file, and confirm `.txt` is permitted. Then re-submit and I'll drive the pipeline immediately.\n2. **Confirm the correct absolute path** — the existence check found nothing at the given path.\n3. **Submit the document as a raw text stream** instead of a path; ingestion can then validate, read byte-exact, and chunk deterministically.\n\nOnce the file is reachable, the sequence is: I establish `document_id`, `page_units`, `total_pages`, and the pinned ruleset → route each page to detection + HITL review **in strict page order, one page in flight at a time**, holding later pages until each prior page is APPROVE/MODIFY → on a REJECT, route that page back for re-classification and hold the rest → only when 100% of pages are approved do I move to final encode → then verify the hardened artifact before marking COMPLETED.\n\nNo action has been taken on the document, and no state has been advanced."}
