2026-10-15 14:59:18 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:59:18 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Active Learning Agent (Redaction Obfuscation Network)",\n    "Inquiry": "Determine if you are the correct agent to handle per-page human review/approval gating for a document being assessed for redaction at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nI am not the right agent for this inquiry. My scope is the **batch/periodic active-learning loop**: I read an accumulated `feedback_buffer` of structured human decisions (APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT) and edits, aggregate them into per-classifier error patterns (false positives, false negatives, missed entity types, threshold misfires, recurring context), quantify each with evidence counts and confidence, and emit **STAGED** proposals (ADD/REMOVE/ADJUST rule, CHANGE threshold). Those proposals stay inert in the governance store\'s PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue until a Human Admin approves them. I never modify classifier behavior and I do not operate per-request.\n\nPer-page human review/approval gating of a specific document\'s redaction assessment is a **document-level HITL workflow** (per-page review state, approval gating, routing of a single document through human sign-off). I hold none of that state, run on a batch trigger rather than per-document, and cannot read or act on the target file\'s per-page review state. My down-chain agent, the Master Data Classifiers Ruleset System of Record, likewise returned Not Relevant — its only approval gate concerns writes to the classifier ruleset, not document review gating.\n\n(For contrast, what I *can* do: turn accumulated human feedback into staged, evidence-backed classifier-improvement proposals, deduplicate them idempotently across runs, and register each with a stable id in PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW — never auto-applying.)'}
