2026-10-15 14:59:20 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 14:59:20 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\nI consulted my down-chain agent, the Active Learning Agent, and neither it nor its own down-chain (the Master Data Classifiers Ruleset System of Record) claims this inquiry. Per-page human review/approval gating is a document-level HITL workflow, which is outside what we cover.\n\nFor clarity on my own scope: I am the **feedback logging stage** of the redaction workflow. I consume human operator edits captured at a page review gate (MODIFY to add/remove a span, or REJECT) and persist them as append-only, schema-stable training records. I do **not** own the review gate itself, decide, approve, or apply anything, nor operate on per-document review state. Everything I do is downstream of the gate, not the gate.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage (Redaction Obfuscation Network)",\n    "Inquiry": "Determine if you are the correct agent to handle per-page human review/approval gating for a document being assessed for redaction at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n```\n\nI am not the right agent for this inquiry. What I *can* do is record the human edits that result from a page review gate as durable, append-only structured records (page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp) and forward the accumulated structured feedback onward to the learning stage — never applying any classifier change myself. The actual per-page review/approval gating for the document at `/Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt` belongs to a different, document-level HITL review agent.'}
