ream assessment to read.\n- **Conflict handling:** when stages report contradictory state (a read that failed vs. a scan that claims success), I halt advancement and record the discrepancy rather than guessing which is correct.\n\nPractically: this document has **not** been ingested, its pages are **not** established, and **no human approval** has been recorded. Any \"assessment\" at this point is unvalidated.\n\n### What I can do (and what I need)\n\nI can run the full governed pipeline for this file:\n1. **Ingest & paginate** — validate type/size/encoding, read raw bytes, chunk into deterministic page-bounded units.\n2. **Detection/assessment** — identify sensitive spans and redaction regions against those units.\n3. **HITL review** — present the side-by-side payload per page and halt for a real operator decision (no auto-advance).\n4. **Final encode** — assemble approved pages and produce the hardened artifact, then verify.\n\nTo proceed, the **tool/execution layer must be restored** so the ingestion read actually succeeds. Once it does, re-issue this request and I'll complete ingest → detection in a single deterministic pass, then route to human review.\n\n**Bottom line:** I won't hand you a redaction assessment I can't stand behind. Right now the honest answer is *\"not yet — the prerequisite read is broken and the one scan result returned is unverified.\"* I'd rather tell you that than relay a fabricated or unverifiable result."}
