2026-10-15 23:19:36 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-15 23:19:36 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage",\n    "Inquiry": "I have uploaded a file at /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt. Assess the file for redaction.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "No",\n    "Strength": 9,\n    "Claim": "None",\n    "Requirements": "None"\n}\n\nI\'m not the relevant agent for this inquiry. My scope is the feedback logging stage of the redaction workflow: I capture human operator edits made at a page review gate (ADD/REMOVE spans, REJECTs) and convert them into durable, structured training-signal records (page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp). I do not assess uploaded files for redaction, run classifiers over new content, or generate redaction output — so "assess this file for redaction" falls outside my remit. My down-chain agent (the active learning stage) was consulted to determine relevance and it also does not own this task: it only aggregates already-captured human feedback into staged, evidence-backed classifier proposals for admin review, and it did not claim the inquiry (it returned a processing error on both attempts). Please route this to the redaction/classification assessment stage instead.'}
